e1: root-config -> extension-runtime selects note="The root file names every extension that loads. Nothing is discovered."
e2: extension-meta -> extension-runtime shapes note="Metadata declares slots, requirements, and fallbacks."
e3: capability-name -> extension-runtime shapes note="Capability strings decide conflicts and load order."
e4: storage-namespace -> extension-runtime shapes note="Core assigns each extension its own durable directory."
e5: extension-runtime -> extension-app registers note="One instance per extension, created once at start."
e6: extension-app -> route-registrar registers note="An extension declares a route prefix here."
e7: extension-app -> markdown-registrar registers note="An extension claims a fence marker here."
e8: extension-app -> asset-registrar registers note="An extension declares its bundles here."
e9: route-registrar -> core-app feeds note="Validated routes reach the real application."
e10: markdown-registrar -> fence-handler claims note="One marker, exactly one owning extension."
e11: asset-registrar -> asset-url feeds note="Core publishes the URL; the extension never invents one."
e12: core-app -> asgi-app serves note="Start-up is done. The callable is ready for traffic."
e13: extension-runtime -> layout-extension selects note="At most one. Boot fails if none is active."
e14: extension-runtime -> search-extension selects note="If it breaks, core disables search and keeps serving."
e15: extension-runtime -> tasks-extension selects note="Switching it off removes the graph fence entirely."
e16: asgi-app -> content-route routes_to note="A document URL reaches its handler."
e17: beforeware -> content-route gates note="Runs before every handler, on every request."
e18: rbac -> content-route gates note="A denied path stops here. Nothing below runs."
e19: content-route -> content-mounts resolves note="A slug becomes a root and a relative path."
e20: content-mounts -> content-backend reads note="Ask for a document without knowing where it lives."
e21: content-backend -> filesystem-backend picks note="The working tree, when no ref is asked for."
e22: content-backend -> git-backend picks note="A committed ref, when the URL names one."
e23: git-backend -> virtual-path serves note="Git objects wearing a path-shaped interface."
e24: filesystem-backend -> markdown-file reads note="The bytes of one document."
e25: markdown-file -> frontmatter feeds note="The metadata block comes off the top."
e26: frontmatter -> from-md shapes note="Title, width, and per-page switches."
e27: folder-config -> from-md shapes note="A subtree can tune rendering without touching the root."
e28: from-md -> fence-handler routes_to note="A fenced block goes to whichever extension claimed the marker."
e29: fence-handler -> kg-pack reads note="The items fence loads a graph pack from disk."
e30: kg-pack -> tasks-extension feeds note="The pack becomes the model the canvas draws."
e31: from-md -> wikilink-resolver routes_to note="Double-bracket links are resolved during render."
e32: wikilink-resolver -> content-mounts reads note="A link is checked against the same mounts the router uses."
e33: from-md -> asset-collector feeds note="Whatever rendered records the bundles this page needs."
e34: asset-collector -> asset-url resolves note="Bundle names become URLs the page can reference."
e35: from-md -> page-frame renders note="The body, and the chrome it asked for."
e36: layout-extension -> page-shell shapes note="Page structure and navigation surfaces."
e37: page-frame -> page-shell wraps note="Head, navbar, sidebar, footer close around the body."
e38: page-shell -> html-response renders note="A full document, or an htmx fragment."
e39: html-response -> asset-url reads note="The page references the CSS and JS it was given."
e40: asset-url -> asgi-app routes_to note="The browser asks for the asset on a core-managed URL."
e41: asgi-app -> asset-registrar reads note="Core looks up which extension owns that bundle."
e42: asset-registrar -> tasks-extension reads note="Bytes come from the extension's own directory."
e43: tasks-extension -> html-response feeds note="The canvas script reaches the page that asked for it."
e44: markdown-file -> reload-hub notifies note="A saved document wakes the watcher."
e45: kg-pack -> reload-hub notifies note="Editing any file in a pack counts as one change."
e46: reload-hub -> html-response notifies note="Open pages are told what changed."
e47: html-response -> content-route routes_to note="The page asks for itself again. The loop closes."
e48: search-extension -> content-mounts reads note="The index is built from the same mounts."
